  "term": "ancillary",
  "definition": "In this psychology-of-performance context, ancillary refers to body movements that are not directly needed to produce the main action or outcome, such as sound, but that may still relate to structure, expression, and how others perceive the performance. The packet supports this meaning specifically for piano performance.",
